  "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story. Asset type: Japanese elementary vocabulary illustrations, sheet 25. Edit the provided 2048x2048 template, painting ONLY inside its sixteen white panels. Every single panel MUST have identical width and height. All horizontal lines must be EXACTLY at 0%,25%,50%,75%,100%, not based on artwork. Keep precisely the 4x4 equal grid and 5 continuous pure magenta #ff00ff lines in each direction, including outer frame. Preserve line position, width and full canvas. Each panel is an independent clear gentle picture-book illustration as isolated vignettes on a pure white background, large and easily understood. Never use magenta for illustration. Avoid all pink, purple and neon colors in artwork, objects, decorations, lighting and shadows. Use warm orange, red, yellow, green, blue and neutral colors. No pink/purple concert lights. Nothing crosses the grid. No text, letters, numbers, labels, symbols resembling writing or watermarks. For abstract words show a concrete situation illustrating the meaning. Diverse natural children and adults, no stereotypes. Correct anatomy and objects. Panels in strict row-major order (left to right, top to bottom):\n1. カリキュラム — 学ぶ内容や順序を組み立てた計画。\n2. カルシウム — 骨や歯を作る成分にもなる元素。\n3. カルテ — 診察や治療の内容を記録するもの。\n4. カルデラ — 火山の活動でできる大きなくぼ地。\n5. カレンダー — 月や日や曜日が分かるように並べた表。\n6. カレーライス — カレーをかけたごはん。\n7. カロリー — 熱量を表す単位。食べ物のエネルギーにも使うよ。\n8. 川岸 — 川の水が流れている所のすぐそば。\n9. 革靴 — 革を主な材料にして作った靴。\n10. 考え — 頭の中で思ったことや判断したこと。\n11. 考え方 — 物事をどのように受け取って考えるかという方法。\n12. カンガルー — 大きな後ろ足で跳ねる有袋類の動物。\n13. 観客 — 試合や舞台などを見に来た人。\n14. 緩急 — ゆっくりしていることと速いこと。\n15. 環境保護 — 自然や暮らしの環境を守ること。\n16. 観光客 — 景色や名所などを見に訪れる人。\nSafety and clarity: Vehicles must be driven only by unmistakable adults, never children. Industrial machinery and knives are used by adults. Do not put a child in a car driver's seat. Keep artwork separated by the measured template grid.\n",
